## Troubleshooting

### CUDA Out of Memory
```bash
# Reduce inference steps
--num_inference_steps 30
```

### Driver Issues
```bash
# Check driver
nvidia-smi

# Reinstall if needed
sudo apt-get purge nvidia-*
sudo apt-get install -y nvidia-driver-535
sudo reboot
```

### PyTorch Not Detecting GPU
```bash
# Verify CUDA installation
nvcc --version
python3 -c "import torch; print(torch.cuda.is_available())"

# Reinstall PyTorch
pip uninstall torch torchvision torchaudio
pip install torch torchvision torchaudio --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu121
```

## Cost Optimization

The VM auto-starts and auto-stops via your local `wan_client.py`. To manually manage:

```bash
# Stop VM (saves costs)
gcloud compute instances stop video-gen-vm --zone=us-central1-a

# Start VM
gcloud compute instances start video-gen-vm --zone=us-central1-a
```

**Estimated costs:**
- **Spot pricing**: ~$1.10/hour
- **Per video**: ~$0.010 (30 seconds generation)
- **100 videos/month**: ~$1.00

